  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Beyond Compliance Consortium Research Programme &#x2013; Building Evidence on Promoting Restraint by Armed Actors</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of this theoretical, empirical and operational research programme is to contribute to the effective prevention and reduction of civilian harm in armed conflict and facilitate a broader protective environment. This will be achieved by improving the strategic understanding and operational and policy know-how of key stakeholders on what interventions are most effective in generating compliance and promoting restraint by armed actors. The programme&#x2019;s  main contributions will be: i) a solid qualitative and quantitative empirical evidence base that is anchored in, and iteratively informs, ii) a contextualizable theoretical framework on how compliance and restraint by armed actors can prevent, reduce and respond to need and harm caused by war; both of which will underpin iii) actionable and actor-targeted research outputs, with policy and wider societal impact conceived transversally throughout, and beyond the lifespan of the research.</narrative>
  </description>
